.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VOP_LOOKUP 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_lookup
.Nd lookup a component name in a directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_lookup "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "const char *name" "struct ucred *cred"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vop_lookup
function searches the directory
.Fa dvp
for the directory entry
.Fa name .
If found, the associated vnode is returned in
.Fa *vpp
with a reference count incremented.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa cred"
.It Fa dvp
The directory vnode to search.
.It Fa vpp
Pointer to a vnode pointer where the result will be stored.
.It Fa name
The component name to look up.
.It Fa cred
The user credentials for the operation.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width ".Bq Er ENOENT"
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
The vnode
.Fa dvp
is not a directory.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
The component
.Fa name
was not found in the directory.
.It Bq Er EACCES
Permission denied.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The filesystem does not support this operation.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_cachedlookup 9
